Sidekick Codex plugin

Install:
  On first installation, validate bundled skills and assemble the plugin with the current Archify and PPT Master tool resources.
  For an existing installation, preserve plugin files; use wsley upgrade sidekick to synchronize bundled skills and upstream tool resources.
  Prepare and verify managed environments, register the Wsley local marketplace and enable Sidekick, including a previously disabled installation.
  Refresh the managed Mira instruction and set agents.max_concurrent_threads_per_session to 20 while preserving unrelated configuration.

Upgrade:
  Skip the operation when Sidekick is not installed.
  Assemble bundled skills and latest upstream tool resources, synchronize dependencies and verify environments before replacing the plugin.
  Refresh registration and managed configuration, set the agent thread limit to 20 and enable Sidekick even if it was previously disabled.

Status:
  Report plugin registration, upstream tool records, managed Codex configuration, browser and MCP package versions, Chromium binding, presentation dependencies and system packages.
  Run bounded local diagnostics without installing, upgrading or probing external services; skip the live browser launch test.

Requirements:
  Ubuntu, APT, AWK, an installed Codex CLI with plugin marketplace commands and a regular user with sudo access.
  Installation and upgrades require network access to the relevant GitHub, npm, Python, Chromium and APT sources.

Configuration:
  Marketplace root: ${XDG_DATA_HOME:-$HOME/.local/share}/sidekick
  Plugin source: ${XDG_DATA_HOME:-$HOME/.local/share}/sidekick/plugin
  Plugin registration: sidekick@wsley; installed plugin files are managed by the Codex plugin cache.
  Codex configuration: ${CODEX_HOME:-$HOME/.codex}/config.toml
  Managed environments: ${XDG_DATA_HOME:-$HOME/.local/share}/sidekick/runtimes

  Entry skill: sidekick:mira; describe project work naturally, with task coordination and specialist routing maintained in its skill files.
  Bundled skills are maintained in assets/sidekick/skills and use the host's default automatic selection; upgrades preserve these local methods rather than replacing them with upstream instructions.
  Each skill uses name and description frontmatter, agents/openai.yaml interface metadata and a LICENSE containing applicable terms and upstream references with full commit hashes.
  assets/upstream.json declares complete version-coupled tool resources under vendor/<name>, preserving their original instructions, scripts, templates and licenses.
  Assembly uses project-scoped pnpx skills@latest with --copy; each repository HEAD is resolved once unless an explicit revision and pin_reason document a compatibility constraint.
  skills-lock.json records acquired tool commits and hashes; later upgrades resolve current sources without reusing this record as a version pin.

  Browser and draw.io MCP packages use published versions recorded in runtime-packages.json; the generated mcp.json calls the managed executable directly.
  The browser CLI provides version-matched instructions and installs Chromium with Linux dependencies; activation includes an offline launch test.
  Archify uses the validated runtimes/chromium link with ARCHIFY_CHROME and ARCHIFY_UPDATE_CHECK_DISABLED=1; an unchanged binding is preserved.
  Presentations use a managed Python 3.12 environment, vendor/ppt-master/requirements.txt and the system tools declared in components.tsv.
  Reuse a valid presentation interpreter and rebuild a missing, damaged or incorrectly versioned environment; reject symlinked runtime directories and replace environment symlinks without following them.
  Environments are prepared by Wsley commands and used directly by skills; project toolchains, dependencies, accounts, keys and remote services remain project or task configuration.

  Manage one <wsley-sidekick>...</wsley-sidekick> block in developer_instructions, preserving user text outside it and instructing Mira to resume unfinished work after compaction or handoffs.
  Installation and upgrade set agents.max_concurrent_threads_per_session to 20 spawned-agent threads, excluding the primary thread; preserve other settings, custom roles and TOML comments.
  Reject invalid Codex configuration before preparing runtime environments; skip managed configuration writes when values do not change.
  Back up existing targets before changes, preserving symlinks as links; restore plugin files and configuration if activation fails.
  Assembly or environment validation failure leaves plugin files and configuration untouched; completed dependency changes remain and no older upstream version is substituted.
  Browser downloads and Python interpreter caches follow their tools' storage settings; global skill directories are not modified.
  Open a new Codex conversation after installation or upgrade to load the plugin and entry instruction.
